      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given:\n\\[ VB = \\sqrt{13}, \\quad VB = 3 \\]\nWe are tasked with finding $\\tan V = \\frac{2028}{6070}$, where $VB = 2028$ and $BK = 6070$. Our goal is to calculate the ratio $\\frac{2028}{6070}$.\n\nTo achieve this, we need to investigate triangle $BVW$. \n\nFirst, we relate $WY$ to $YW$ using the following relation:\n\\[ WY \\cdot YB = WY \\cdot YW \\]\n\nBased on the given information, we have:\n\\[ 2WY = 1 \\Rightarrow WY = \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet's use the ratio between $YB$ and $WY$ to calculate $\\tan V$:\n\\[ \\tan V = \\frac{WY}{YB} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1} = \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nTherefore, option C, which is $\\frac{1}{2}$, is the correct answer. \n\nThis means that $\\tan V = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}$.\n\nThe students are going camping and Mr. Sampson has lead 10 boys in 2 separate rock climbing conditions where 1 boy got injured. However, to win the camping trip while recovering, a boy needs to be present in each climbing condition while still recovering. How many boys are not recovering in the 2 climbing conditions now. Note that, some of the injured boys might be able to recover at the next experiment. Also, assume that out of 10 boys, 2 have always been recovering from low heights.\nFirst, let's formalize the problem. We know that there are 10 boys, with 2 of them recovering from low heights. This means there are \\(10 - 2 = 8\\) boys who are not recovering from low heights. \n\nNow we need to determine how many of these 8 boys are still recovering. Since 1 boy got injured in one climbing condition, and he will need to be present in each climbing condition while recovering, only that one boy will recover from low heights for the rest of the conditions. \n\nThis means there are 8 boys who are not recovering to begin with, but only 1 of them will be recovering due to the injury. Therefore, the number of boys who are not recovering after the condition is:\n\\[ 8 - 1 = 7 \\]\n\nThus, the number of boys who are not recovering in the 2 climbing conditions is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
