      "text": "Since $VX = \\sqrt{13}$ and $VW = 3$, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find $WX$ as follows:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}WX &= \\sqrt{VX^2 - VW^2} \\\\&= \\sqrt{13 - 9} \\\\&= 2.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince $\\angle VWX = 90^\\circ$, we can conclude that\n$$\\frac{VW}{WX} = \\sqrt{\\frac{WX^2}{VX^2}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}.$$\n\nSince $\\tan$ is the ratio of $\\sin$ to $\\cos$, we have\n$$\\frac{\\tan V}{\\cos V} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}.$$\n\nIt follows that $\\tan V = \\boxed{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}}.$\n\nNote: $\\sin V = \\tan V \\sin X = \\frac{\\tan V}{\\cos V} \\sin X = \\frac{\\tan^2 V}{1 + \\tan^2 V} \\sin X,$\n\nso $\\sin X = -\\frac{\\tan^2 V}{1 + \\tan^2 V} \\cdot \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} = \\frac{\\tan V}{\\sqrt{13}}.$",
